From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Priyadharshini Gowthaman <pgowtham@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 17:28:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] UPSTREAM:PROTOCOL: sigma_dut: Set ath12k ba_mode Manual for ADDBA reject

Squashed with the follow-up fixup patch: uses cfg80211tool
directly per the reference's final verified implementation,
skipping the intermediate debugfs approach the fixup patch
replaced.

Signed-off-by: Priyadharshini Gowthaman <pgowtham@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
diff --git a/ap.c b/ap.c
index f1f1a68..06cef1c 100644
--- a/ap.c
+++ b/ap.c
@@ -11203,6 +11203,21 @@ static void fwtest_set_eht_params(struct sigma_dut *dut, const char *ifname,
 			    dut->ap_addba_reject == VALUE_ENABLED) ? 0 : 1,
 			   ifname);

+	/* ath12k: FW default BA mode is Auto (0) — FW negotiates BA
+	 * sessions on its own without going through mac80211's ADDBA Req
+	 * processing path, so the addba_req_enable knob above never gets
+	 * a chance to block it.  Switch this link to Manual mode (1) via
+	 * cfg80211tool so BA session control is left to the
+	 * host when ADDBA_REJECT,enable is in effect; restore to Auto (0)
+	 * otherwise. */
+	if (strncmp(dut->device_driver, "ath12k", 6) == 0) {
+		run_system_wrapper(dut,
+				   "cfg80211tool %s ba_mode %d",
+				   ifname,
+				   (dut->ap_ampdu == VALUE_DISABLED &&
+				    dut->ap_addba_reject == VALUE_ENABLED) ? 1 : 0);
+	}
+
 	/* mac80211/ath12k: trigger beacon reconvergence after all bss_he_* and
 	 * bss_eht_* SET calls above have updated the hostapd capability state. */
 	run_system_wrapper(dut, "hostapd_cli -i %s UPDATE_BEACON", ifname);
